# J1 — Keyless first launch (⭐ highest priority)
# Persona: brand-new user, no credentials. Walk the ordered gate
# Target → Model → Credentials, then take the `d` offline-demo escape hatch.
# Known risk (July): credential dead-end dumped the operator on an empty
# Workbench instead of the inline credential-entry step.
name: Keyless first launch
note: HOME is redirected to a temp dir. Keychain/OAuth-cached credentials cannot be masked from here — if the auth gate never appears, check for cached credentials before judging.
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY OPENROUTER_API_KEY GEMINI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 2 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: target-gate
expect: Nothing defaults to cwd silently
expect: offline fixture
ask: Target gate — is the operator told WHY they are stopped here, and is the next action obvious without docs?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 2 CHOOSE A MODEL
snap: model-gate
expect: does not silently pick a model
ask: Model gate — can a keyless user tell which rows are usable right now vs. which need credentials they do not have?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 15 CHOOSE AUTH METHOD
snap: credentials-gate
expect: needs credentials
expect: Offline demo
ask: Credentials gate — July regression check: does the keyless user get an inline credential-entry step (paste / OAuth / demo) rather than being dumped on an empty Workbench?
keys: d
wait-for: 90 run completed
snap: offline-demo-result
expect: findings
ask: Offline escape hatch — did `d` make a real scanner signal, redacted location, and signal_only proof state legible, not just dump logs?
